diagnosis_text:
Affected component: router2’s Server Room gateway interface (eth0) IP addressing. The interface is configured as 1.0.0.1/8 instead of the intended /30 subnet.

Mechanism: pc1 is on 1.0.0.5/30 (network 1.0.0.4/30). With router2’s eth0 set to 1.0.0.1/8, the two ends are on mismatched subnets. pc1 treats 1.0.0.1 as off-link (not in 1.0.0.4/30), so it cannot properly establish a default route via that IP and cannot return traffic to 1.0.0.1. Conversely, router2 thinks 1.0.0.5 is directly connected (/8) and ARPs for it, so ARP tables look “REACHABLE” on both sides, but ICMP echo fails because pc1 has no valid route for replies.

Localization and evidence:
- pc1: 1.0.0.5/30 on eth0, no default route; ip neigh shows 1.0.0.
